# Crypto analysis (domain)

## When to use
- Groq analysis output shape, bias/action rules, or timeframe interpretation
- Signal gate / setup grading context (see `setup-gate.analyzer.ts`, `signal-gate.service.ts`)

## Timeframe priority
`4h` > `1d` > `1h` > `15m` (HTF bias drives decisions)

## Active method
- **`kim_nghia`**: active; confidence thresholds from env (`KIM_NGHIA_CONFIDENCE_THRESHOLD`, default ~0.82 for actions)
- **`ict`**: disabled in `config/methods.ts` but schema/prompts preserved

## Consistency rules
- `bullish` → `buy`; `bearish` → `sell`; `neutral` → `hold`
- Long: `stop_loss < entry < take_profit`; short: `take_profit < entry < stop_loss`
- Position decisions must align with bias (see tests in `biasConsistencyValidation.test.js`)

## LLM JSON (Kim Nghia / ICT prompts)
- Raw JSON only — no markdown fences or prose outside `{...}`
- BTC object includes `bias`, `action`, `confidence`, `suggested_*`, optional `position_decisions` / `pending_order_decisions`

## Pipeline (v3)
Market scan → **Signal gate** → **Risk engine** → **Groq dispatch** → testnet execution (when enabled). Do not bypass gate/risk via env flags.

## Verification
- [ ] Output validates against prompt rules in `config/methods.ts`
- [ ] `method_id` stored and queried consistently in DB/API
